			"notes": "Tool Belt Unlimited 1.5.1 adds a configurable inventory grid and matching concentric selection rings, including a fix for inserting held items into a specific empty slot.\n\n- Configure slots per inventory row/ring with server setting `itemsPerRing` (default 9, range 1–24).\n- Enable or disable rings with client setting `useRings`; limit simultaneously visible rings with `maxVisibleRings` (default 3).\n- Scroll through ring layers in both directions, wrapping around and skipping hidden rows.\n- Use the eye beside each inventory row to hide or restore it in ring selection. Preferences are saved per belt and survive upgrades.\n- Fix selective insertion into empty ring slots when Tool Belt's empty-slot display is disabled. Center insertion and occupied-slot swapping remain available.\n\nRequires Minecraft 1.21.1, NeoForge, Tool Belt 2.2.9, Sewing Kit 2.0.9, and Kotlin for Forge 5.10+. Install the addon on client and server.\n\nValidation: successful build, in-game inventory/ring tests with an integrated server, configuration and eye-button checks, and a reproduced-then-fixed selective-insertion test covering mouse click, key release and scrolled ring layers. No long-term dedicated multiplayer test was performed."
		},
